# Cloudflare Static Assets header rules. Copied verbatim into build/web by
# `flutter build web`, and consumed as configuration rather than served.
#
# Deliberately NO `immutable` rules. That is the obvious optimisation here and
# it is wrong: Flutter web does not content-hash its output. Every filename is
# stable across builds — assets/FontManifest.json, assets/fonts/*.otf,
# canvaskit/canvaskit.wasm, even main.dart.js — so a long immutable max-age
# pins returning visitors to the previous build's assets until it expires.
# Cloudflare's default (`max-age=0, must-revalidate`) is already correct for
# those: the browser revalidates and gets a 304 when nothing changed.
#
# What is worth overriding is the entry points, which name everything else. A
# cached copy of any of them survives a deploy and keeps loading the old app.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

/flutter_service_worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate

/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-store, must-revalidate
